   "source": [
    "# GPU-Accelerated Backtesting Engine\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to use the GPU-Accelerated Backtesting Engine in a Google Colab environment with GPU support.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Ensure you are running this notebook in a Colab environment with GPU runtime enabled\n",
    "2. Install required dependencies\n",
    "3. Build the CUDA-enabled engine\n",
    "4. Run backtesting benchmarks\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Environment Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "First, check if GPU is available and install necessary dependencies:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check GPU availability\n",
    "!nvidia-smi\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install system dependencies\n",
    "!apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3-pip cmake\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install Python dependencies\n",
    "!pip install numpy nanobind\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Clone Repository and Build\n",
    "\n",
    "Clone the repository (if not already done) and build the CUDA-enabled version:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Clone repository (uncomment if needed)\n",
    "# !git clone https://github.com/yourusername/gpu_engine.git\n",
    "# %cd gpu_engine\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build with CUDA enabled\n",
    "!mkdir -p build_cuda && cd build_cuda\n",
    "!cmake .. -DUSE_CUDA=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n",
    "!make -j$(nproc)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Copy the built module to the Python path\n",
    "!cp gpu_engine.so ..\n",
    "%cd ..\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Test the Engine\n",
    "\n",
    "Verify that the engine is working correctly with synthetic data:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add current directory to path\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    import gpu_engine as ge\n",
    "    print(\"✓ Successfully imported gpu_engine module\")\n",
    "except ImportError as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"✗ Failed to import gpu_engine: {e}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Make sure the module is built and in the Python path\")\n",
    "    sys.exit(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "def generate_test_data(n_points=10000):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generate synthetic test data\"\"\"\n",
    "    np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Generate timestamps (nanoseconds)\n",
    "    timestamps = np.arange(n_points, dtype=np.uint64) * 1000000000  # 1 second intervals\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Generate prices with some random walk\n",
    "    returns = np.random.normal(0, 0.01, n_points)  # 1% volatility\n",
    "    prices = 100 * np.exp(np.cumsum(returns))  # Start at $100\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Generate volumes\n",
    "    volumes = np.random.uniform(100, 1000, n_points)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return timestamps, prices, volumes\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nGenerating test data...\")\n",
    "timestamps, prices, volumes = generate_test_data(5000)\n",
    "print(f\"Data shape: {len(timestamps)} points\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Creating FastQuantEngine...\")\n",
    "engine = ge.FastQuantEngine(\n",
    "    timestamps.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    prices.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    volumes.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    len(timestamps)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Running parameter sweep...\")\n",
    "results = engine.run_parameter_sweep(\n",
    "    fast_window_range=(5, 20),\n",
    "    slow_window_range=(20, 50),\n",
    "    slippage_bps=1.5,\n",
    "    commission_bps=0.5\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    f\"Got {len(results)} results\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst 5 results:\")\n",
    "for i, result in enumerate(results[:5]):\n",
    "    print(f\"Result {i}: P&L={result.total_pnl:.2f}, Sharpe={result.sharpe_ratio:.2f}, \"\n",
    "          f\"DD={result.max_drawdown:.2f}%, Trades={result.total_trades}, Win%={result.win_rate:.1f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Basic validation\n",
    "assert len(results) > 0, \"Should have results\"\n",
    "assert all(isinstance(r.total_pnl, float) for r in results), \"P&L should be float\"\n",
    "assert all(isinstance(r.total_trades, int) for r in results), \"Trades should be int\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ Basic functionality test passed!\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Performance Benchmark\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare performance between CPU and GPU implementations (when available):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "def benchmark_engine(engine, fast_range, slow_range, slippage=1.5, commission=0.5):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Benchmark the engine performance\"\"\"\n",
    "    start_time = time.time()\n",
    "    results = engine.run_parameter_sweep(fast_range, slow_range, slippage, commission)\n",
    "    end_time = time.time()\n",
    "    return end_time - start_time, len(results)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate larger dataset for meaningful benchmark\n",
    "print(\"Generating larger test dataset (50K points)...\")\n",
    "timestamps_large, prices_large, volumes_large = generate_test_data(50000)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Creating engine with large dataset...\")\n",
    "engine_large = ge.FastQuantEngine(\n",
    "    timestamps_large.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    prices_large.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    volumes_large.ctypes.data,\n",
    "    len(timestamps_large)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Running benchmark...\")\n",
    "duration, count = benchmark_engine(engine_large, (10, 30), (30, 60))\n",
    "print(f\"Benchmark completed in {duration:.2f} seconds\")\n",
    f\"Evaluated {count} parameter combinations\"\n",
    f\"Performance: {count/duration:.1f} combinations/second\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Saving and Loading Results\n",
    "\n",
    "Example of how to save backtesting results for further analysis:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert results to DataFrame for easy analysis\n",
    "results_data = []\n",
    "for i, result in enumerate(results):\n",
    "    results_data.append({\n",
    "        'result_id': i,\n",
    "        'total_pnl': result.total_pnl,\n",
    "        'sharpe_ratio': result.sharpe_ratio,\n",
    "        'max_drawdown': result.max_drawdown,\n",
    "        'total_trades': result.total_trades,\n",
    "        'win_rate': result.win_rate\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(results_data)\n",
    "print(\"Results DataFrame shape:\", df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save to CSV\n",
    "df.to_csv('backtesting_results.csv', index=False)\n",
    "print(\"\\nResults saved to backtesting_results.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show basic statistics\n",
    "print(\"\\nResults Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(df.describe())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Cleanup\n",
    "\n",
    "Remove temporary files and collected garbage:"
